    <h2>Hi, I'm {{ site.consultantName }} 👋</h2>
    <p>I'm {{ site.consultantName }}, a Thermomix®️ Independent Consultant based in the Toronto Area, serving buyers across Canada. I'm a foodie who loves eating, discovering new cuisines, and trying new foods—but I'm not someone who wants to spend hours in the kitchen to make a good meal.</p>
    <p>I also wasn't a particularly confident cook. So when I first discovered the TM7, what caught my attention wasn't just everything it could do—it was how much easier it made cooking feel, especially when you're not someone who naturally knows what to do in the kitchen.</p>
    <p>I was sold after a demo where the TM7 prepared a full multi-course meal at once, using its different levels to cook a protein, side, soup, and rice simultaneously. I couldn't believe how much one machine could actually do.</p>
    <p>Since then, it's become a regular part of our family kitchen. I've made everything from congee and dumpling fillings to curries, pasta and desserts. My daughters have gone from watching me cook to choosing recipes and making them themselves. And my mother-in-law, who had mostly cooked Asian food her whole life, is now regularly exploring recipes and cuisines from around the world.</p>
    <h2>Why I Created This Site</h2>
    <p>When I was researching the TM7, there was no shortage of official information about what it could do. What I found harder to find was something more personal: What is it actually like to use one as an Asian family in Canada? Does it work for the food we grew up eating? Is it useful if you're not a confident cook? And after spending over $2,000, is it really worth it?</p>
    <p>That's what I wanted this site to be.</p>
    <p>A straightforward, personal look at the TM7 from someone who actually uses it at home. I'll share what I love, what surprised me, where I think it falls short, and—perhaps most importantly—who I don't think needs one.</p>
    <p>No pressure. Just an honest look at whether the TM7 is right for you, your cooking style, and your family.</p>
    <p>And if you decide it is, you can purchase through my consultant link, with the shipping fee automatically waived.</p>
